    intro = @(
      "Aston Martin occupies a singular position in the automotive world — a small, independent British manufacturer producing hand-crafted grand tourers and sports cars that blend extraordinary performance with bespoke elegance. In Dubai, the Aston Martin is a statement of refined taste rather than mere wealth, and owners expect their cars to perform flawlessly in a climate that was never part of the original engineering brief. The DBX, Aston Martin's first SUV, has significantly expanded the brand's presence in the UAE market, bringing first-time Aston Martin owners who may not be familiar with the brand's specific maintenance requirements.",
      "Every Aston Martin sold in the UAE is built around a hand-assembled Mercedes-AMG derived V8 or a bespoke twin-turbocharged V12. These engines are calibrated for performance and refinement above all else, and they demand lubricants, fluids and service intervals that reflect this priority. In Dubai's ambient temperatures of 45°C or above, the cooling and lubrication demands on these high-output engines are extreme. Oil temperature management is particularly critical — synthetic lubricants must be renewed on schedule, and the engine's dry-sump system requires careful inspection at every service.",
      "The DBX uses an AMG-derived 4.0-litre twin-turbo V8 producing 550 hp, mated to a nine-speed automatic transmission. In Dubai, this platform faces the same thermal challenges as its AMG counterparts but with additional complexity from Aston Martin's own chassis tuning software and adaptive suspension systems. The sports cars — DB11, Vantage and DBS — sit lower and run hotter; in summer traffic their cooling systems operate near design limits for extended periods, making thermostat condition, coolant quality and radiator integrity critical safety items.",
      "At FixHive, our technicians have experience with Aston Martin's AMG-derived platforms as well as the older V8 Vantage and DB9 models still common in the UAE. We use genuine or approved OEM-equivalent parts, follow Aston Martin service specifications precisely, and maintain full service records for every visit. For Aston Martin owners who want dealer-quality care without the extended wait times and premium pricing of the franchised network, FixHive offers a genuine alternative in Dubai."
    )
    issues = @(
      @{ title = "V8 AMG Engine Overheating in Dubai Summer Traffic"; body = "The AMG-derived 4.0-litre twin-turbocharged V8 fitted to the DB11, Vantage, DBS and DBX is an extraordinarily capable engine, but its high specific output means it generates substantial heat even at moderate loads. In Dubai summer traffic — where ambient temperatures regularly exceed 45°C and cars sit idling for extended periods — the cooling system operates at or near its design maximum. The twin turbines add significant heat soak to the engine bay, and the inter-cooler circuit must reject additional heat on top of the primary coolant loop. Symptoms of cooling stress include the temperature gauge sitting higher than usual in slow traffic, occasional cooling fan running after engine shutdown, and in advanced cases an overheating warning. We recommend coolant inspection and replacement every 2 years, a thermostat test at every major service, and ensuring the front splitter and undertray are intact to preserve designed airflow." },
      @{ title = "Transmission Software and Adaptive Suspension Calibration"; body = "Aston Martin's ZF-derived 8-speed and 9-speed automatic transmissions contain manufacturer-specific calibration software that controls shift mapping, torque converter lockup and launch control. This software is not accessible via standard OBD-II diagnostic tools — it requires Aston Martin's proprietary diagnostic system or compatible specialist equipment. In Dubai, the transmission faces additional stress from high ambient temperatures and the aggressive driving styles common on UAE highways. Adaptive damper systems — standard on DBX and optional on DB11 — also require periodic recalibration checks, particularly after suspension work. At FixHive we carry specialist diagnostic capability for AMG-platform Aston Martins and can read, clear and log manufacturer-specific fault codes across all control modules." },
      @{ title = "Paint, PPF and Exterior Finish Degradation in UAE Climate"; body = "Aston Martin's paint finishes are among the most complex and expensive in the automotive industry. Many models leave the factory with up to 12 layers of paint applied by hand, and special finishes — Satin, Brushed Aluminium, Carbon Black — require specialist care that is entirely different from standard automotive paintwork. In Dubai, UV radiation at ground level is among the highest in the world, and extended exposure without paint protection film or ceramic coating causes irreversible fading and oxidisation of even the deepest metallic finishes. The front bumper, bonnet and door edges are also vulnerable to stone chips on UAE highways, where road debris and truck tyre fragments are a constant hazard. We strongly recommend full-vehicle PPF installation for all Aston Martin models driven in Dubai, along with an annual ceramic coating maintenance regime." },
      @{ title = "Brake System Wear on High-Performance Variants"; body = "The carbon-ceramic brake option fitted to Vantage AMR, DBS Superleggera and performance-specification DB11 models is a high-temperature braking system designed for track use, but owners in Dubai frequently use these cars on extended motorway journeys and in hot urban traffic. Carbon-ceramic discs are brittle at low temperatures — they perform best above 200°C — and in normal Dubai city driving they may never reach operating temperature, causing micro-cracking of the disc surface over time. Standard cast-iron brake systems on entry Vantage and DBX models wear faster in Dubai due to the sand and dust that acts as an abrasive on pad faces and disc surfaces. Brake fluid absorbs moisture over time, lowering its boiling point — a critical safety issue on a car capable of 300+ km/h. We recommend brake fluid replacement every 2 years on all Aston Martin models." }
    )
    faqs = @(
      @{ q = "How much does Aston Martin servicing cost in Dubai?"; a = "Minor Aston Martin services at FixHive — oil and filter change, multi-point inspection, fluid top-up — start from AED 800–1,200 depending on the model. Major services covering transmission fluid, coolant renewal, brake inspection and spark plug replacement typically range from AED 2,500–5,000. We provide a full written estimate before any work begins, and all pricing is transparent with no hidden charges." },
      @{ q = "Does FixHive have diagnostic equipment for Aston Martin cars?"; a = "Yes. Our workshop carries specialist diagnostic capability compatible with AMG-platform Aston Martin models including the DB11, Vantage, DBX and DBS. We can read and clear manufacturer-specific fault codes across all modules including the engine, transmission, adaptive suspension, stability control and infotainment systems. Pre-2018 V8 Vantage and DB9 models are also supported via compatible legacy diagnostic tools." },
      @{ q = "Is it safe to service my Aston Martin at an independent garage in Dubai?"; a = "Yes, provided the garage uses correct Aston Martin-specified fluids and OEM-equivalent parts, and follows factory service procedures. Under UAE consumer protection regulations you are not required to use a franchised dealer for scheduled maintenance, and doing so will not void your manufacturer warranty provided proper service records are maintained. FixHive issues a full itemised invoice and service record for every visit." },
      @{ q = "How often should I service an Aston Martin driven in Dubai?"; a = "Aston Martin recommends annual services or every 10,000 miles — we recommend 12-month or 15,000 km intervals in UAE conditions given the heat stress on lubricants. Brake fluid should be renewed every 2 years. Coolant should be inspected annually and replaced every 2 years. The DBX requires a more comprehensive 40,000 km service covering differential and transfer fluid in addition to standard items." },
      @{ q = "What PPF and paint protection do you recommend for Aston Martin in Dubai?"; a = "We recommend full-vehicle paint protection film (PPF) for all Aston Martin models in Dubai, ideally applied before the first highway journey. The UAE's dust, sand, road debris and UV levels are extremely damaging to factory paint finishes. For cars already on the road, a professional decontamination, paint correction if needed, and ceramic coating application is the minimum we recommend. Our detailing team has experience with Aston Martin's hand-painted finishes and specialist colour codes." }
