  @{
    slug = "bentley"
    name = "Bentley"
    models = "Continental GT · Flying Spur · Bentayga · Mulsanne"
    heroSub = "Dubai's specialist for Bentley Continental GT, Flying Spur, Bentayga and Mulsanne. Handcrafted British luxury requires technically exacting care to preserve its performance, finish and residual value."
    intro = @(
      "Bentley represents the pinnacle of British automotive craftsmanship — a marque where every car is assembled by hand in Crewe, England, with an attention to detail that takes weeks to complete on each individual vehicle. In Dubai, Bentley is one of the most visible luxury brands on the road, with the Bentayga SUV particularly popular among UAE buyers who want the brand's extraordinary interior craftsmanship paired with the practicality of a high-riding body. Maintaining a Bentley to the standard its engineering demands requires both the technical expertise to handle its complex systems and the care to preserve its exceptional interior and exterior finishes.",
      "Current Bentley models share much of their underpinning with the Volkswagen Group's highest-tier platforms, with the Continental GT and Flying Spur riding on the MSB platform and using either a 6.0-litre twin-turbocharged W12 or a 4.0-litre twin-turbocharged V8. The Bentayga uses the MLB Evo platform shared with the Audi Q7, Lamborghini Urus and Porsche Cayenne. These platforms are technologically sophisticated — featuring active anti-roll bars, electric rear axle steering, and 48-volt mild-hybrid systems on W12 variants — and require diagnostic equipment that goes well beyond standard OBD-II to properly interrogate.",
      "In Dubai's climate, Bentley's air suspension systems face particular challenges. The Bentayga, Flying Spur and Continental GT all offer air suspension as standard or optional equipment, and Dubai's temperature extremes cause air spring rubber bladders to harden and crack over time, leading to slow leaks that first manifest as a slightly lower ride height on one corner in the morning. This is a known wear item in the UAE market. The W12 engine — a masterpiece of engineering with its 12 cylinders arranged in a W configuration — requires immaculate lubrication to maintain its extraordinarily low noise, vibration and harshness characteristics.",
      "At FixHive, we approach every Bentley service with the reverence the car deserves. Our technicians follow Volkswagen Group service procedures for the underlying platforms and use Bentley-approved fluids and OEM-equivalent parts throughout. We maintain full service documentation and can carry out the complete scheduled maintenance programme — including software updates via our VW Group diagnostic tools — so that your Bentley's service history remains comprehensive and verifiable for future resale."
    )
    issues = @(
      @{ title = "W12 Engine Lubrication and Timing Chain Wear"; body = "Bentley's 6.0-litre W12 engine is an engineering marvel — twelve cylinders arranged in a W configuration, twin-turbocharged, producing up to 635 hp in the Speed specification. Its complexity is matched by its sensitivity to lubrication quality. The W12 uses a timing chain system rather than a belt, but the chains require precise oil pressure and viscosity to maintain correct camshaft timing across all four banks. In Dubai, where engine oil degrades faster due to sustained high ambient temperatures and the frequent cold starts that occur throughout the hot season (air conditioning compressor loads the engine heavily from the first moment of startup), oil change intervals should be shortened from the European 15,000 km recommendation to 10,000 km. Consequences of delayed oil changes on the W12 include stretched timing chains, which produce a distinctive rattling noise at cold startup — a repair that runs to five figures at a Bentley dealer. We recommend Bentley-approved 0W-40 full synthetic oil only, changed every 10,000 km." },
      @{ title = "Air Suspension System Degradation in UAE Temperatures"; body = "The air suspension systems fitted to the Bentayga, Flying Spur and Continental GT are central to the Bentley driving experience — providing the extraordinary combination of ultra-supple ride quality and razor-sharp handling that defines the marque. These systems use rubberised air spring bladders inflated to precise pressures, and Dubai's temperature extremes are particularly aggressive on rubber components. The repeated thermal cycling between 15°C air-conditioned interiors and 50°C exterior temperatures causes the rubber bladder material to harden and develop micro-cracks over several years. The first symptom is typically a slow air leak that causes one corner to sit lower than the others overnight. If left unaddressed, a complete bladder failure at speed can cause the car to suddenly drop onto its bump stops, which is both alarming and potentially dangerous. We inspect air suspension pressure and bladder condition at every major service, and we carry replacement air spring assemblies for common Bentley models." },
      @{ title = "Bentley Interior and Exterior Finish Maintenance in Dubai"; body = "A Bentley's interior is among the most labour-intensive in the automotive world. Hand-stitched leather hides, polished veneer panels, chrome and brushed aluminium trim — each element requires specialist care to maintain its condition in Dubai's environment. The combination of extreme UV levels, fine desert dust, and the humidity spikes of Dubai's brief wet season are particularly destructive. Leather surfaces exposed to direct sunlight through the panoramic glass roof bleach and crack without regular conditioning with Bentley-approved leather care products. Wood veneer and piano black trim panels develop micro-scratches from dust particles during cleaning if incorrect products or cloths are used. Exterior chrome work pits and tarnishes without regular protection. Our detailing team understands Bentley-specific finishes and carries the correct care products for each surface." },
      @{ title = "DCT Dual-Clutch Transmission Hesitation in City Traffic"; body = "The dual-clutch transmission fitted to the Continental GT and Flying Spur — an 8-speed DCT unit developed in conjunction with ZF — is calibrated for smooth, rapid shifts at medium to high speeds. In Dubai's stop-start city traffic, the transmission spends extended periods operating in the low-speed, high-slip zone where the dual clutch packs generate heat without full engagement. Over time, and particularly when the transmission fluid is approaching service age, this results in a characteristic jerkiness or hesitation when pulling away from a standstill or manoeuvring at parking speeds. DCT fluid degradation also accelerates in high ambient temperatures. We recommend transmission fluid replacement every 40,000 km for UAE-driven Continental GT and Flying Spur models, rather than Bentley's global recommendation which does not fully account for UAE traffic conditions." }
    )
    faqs = @(
      @{ q = "How much does Bentley servicing cost in Dubai?"; a = "Minor Bentley services at FixHive — oil and filter change, fluid top-ups, multi-point inspection — start from AED 1,200–2,000 depending on model and engine. W12 models require approximately double the oil volume of a V8, which is reflected in the cost. Major services covering transmission fluid, coolant, spark plugs, air filter and brake inspection typically run AED 4,000–8,000. All costs are confirmed in writing before work begins." },
      @{ q = "How often should I change the oil in my Bentley W12 in Dubai?"; a = "We recommend W12 oil changes every 10,000 km in UAE conditions rather than the European 15,000 km interval. Dubai's sustained high ambient temperatures and frequent cold-start air-conditioning loads degrade synthetic lubricants faster than in temperate climates. Maintaining the correct oil change interval is the single most important thing you can do to protect the W12's timing chain system and ensure its legendary low NVH levels are preserved." },
      @{ q = "Does FixHive have diagnostic tools for Bentley vehicles?"; a = "Yes. Bentley models from 2003 onwards use Volkswagen Group electronic architectures that our VW Group diagnostic tools fully support. This includes the Continental GT (W12 and V8), Flying Spur, and Bentayga. We can read, log and clear fault codes across all modules including the W12 engine management, dual-clutch transmission, air suspension control unit, active anti-roll bars, and infotainment system." },
      @{ q = "Is it safe to service my Bentley at an independent garage in Dubai?"; a = "Yes. UAE consumer protection regulations permit you to have your Bentley maintained at any qualified independent garage without voiding the manufacturer warranty, provided correct fluids, OEM-equivalent parts and factory procedures are used. FixHive issues a full itemised service record for every visit. Many long-term Bentley owners in Dubai use FixHive as their primary service partner due to our faster turnaround times and transparent pricing." },
      @{ q = "What PPF and paint protection do you recommend for Bentley in Dubai?"; a = "Full-vehicle paint protection film is our minimum recommendation for Bentley in Dubai. The Crewe-manufactured paint finishes are exceptional but vulnerable to the UAE's UV levels, road debris and fine dust. For cars with special finishes — Satin, Two-Tone, Carbon Fibre — full PPF is non-negotiable to preserve both appearance and resale value. We also recommend an annual interior leather conditioning treatment and UV-protective window tinting to protect the handstitched interior." }
    )
