  @{
    slug = "byd"
    name = "BYD"
    models = "Atto 3 · Seal · Han · Tang · Dolphin · Sealion"
    heroSub = "Dubai's specialist for BYD electric and plug-in hybrid vehicles. Atto 3, Seal, Han, Tang and Dolphin — advanced EV diagnostics, battery health checks and OTA software support in Dubai."
    intro = @(
      "BYD — Build Your Dreams — has emerged as one of the most significant automotive forces of the 2020s, overtaking Tesla globally in terms of total EV and PHEV sales volume. In the UAE, BYD has established a strong and rapidly growing presence, with the Atto 3 electric SUV becoming one of the best-selling electric vehicles in the country. The brand's combination of competitive pricing, impressive real-world range, and advanced battery technology has made it a genuine mainstream choice rather than a niche curiosity. As BYD's UAE fleet grows, so does the need for technically capable independent service centres that understand the brand's technology.",
      "BYD is unique among automakers in that it manufactures its own battery cells, electric motors, power electronics and vehicle control software — a level of vertical integration that gives it extraordinary control over its product but also creates a more complex service environment. The BYD Blade Battery technology used across the Atto 3, Seal, Han and Dolphin is a lithium iron phosphate (LFP) chemistry in a novel cell-to-pack format that eliminates traditional modules. LFP chemistry is extremely stable and thermally safe — it does not suffer from the thermal runaway risks associated with NMC batteries — but it has different management characteristics that require correct BMS calibration.",
      "In Dubai's climate, BYD electric vehicles face specific challenges around thermal management. The battery pack must be maintained within a precise temperature window for optimal charging speed, range and longevity. BYD's active liquid cooling system handles this effectively, but the cooling fluid requires inspection and replacement on schedule. Importantly, the efficiency penalty of running the cabin air conditioning in Dubai's heat can reduce real-world range by 25-35% compared to European rated figures — a normal and expected characteristic of all EVs in hot climates, not a fault. However, if the battery thermal management system is not functioning correctly, range degradation can be significantly worse.",
      "BYD vehicles also receive over-the-air (OTA) software updates that can modify range, charging curves, regenerative braking behaviour and driver assistance features. At FixHive, our technicians stay current with BYD's software versions and can advise owners on which updates are recommended and which are optional. We carry diagnostic capability for BYD's DiLink infotainment architecture and the underlying vehicle control systems. Our workshop is also equipped to perform AC charging equipment checks and can diagnose DC fast charging communication faults that sometimes arise with third-party chargers in the UAE."
    )
    issues = @(
      @{ title = "Battery Range Degradation and Thermal Management in Dubai Heat"; body = "The BYD Blade Battery is a lithium iron phosphate chemistry known for exceptional cycle life and thermal stability, but all EV batteries lose capacity over time, and Dubai's climate accelerates this process if the thermal management system is not operating correctly. In normal operation, BYD's active liquid cooling maintains battery temperature between 20°C and 40°C even in 50°C ambient heat during fast charging. However, if the cooling circuit develops a blockage, loses fluid, or if the chiller system that pre-cools the battery during DC charging loses performance, battery temperatures can rise above the optimal window. Chronic elevated temperature accelerates LFP capacity fade, and owners may notice gradually increasing charge times and decreasing range. We recommend annual battery health checks at FixHive to baseline capacity, check cooling circuit integrity, inspect the battery management software version, and identify any latent fault codes that have not yet triggered a dashboard warning." },
      @{ title = "Charging System Issues with UAE Third-Party Chargers"; body = "BYD vehicles sold in the UAE use the CCS2 charging standard for DC fast charging and a Type 2 AC connector for home and destination charging. Compatibility issues arise frequently with some UAE-installed DC fast chargers, particularly older OCPP 1.5 protocol chargers at petrol station forecourts and some mall car parks. These incompatibilities typically manifest as a session failing to start, a charge session terminating early at a low state of charge, or the car refusing to communicate with the charger. These are rarely hardware faults — more often they reflect a charger firmware mismatch or a vehicle software version issue. BYD periodically releases charging compatibility updates via OTA. At FixHive we can check and update your vehicle's charging firmware and log diagnostic data from the onboard charging computer to identify persistent compatibility issues." },
      @{ title = "DiLink Infotainment System Freezing and Connectivity Faults"; body = "BYD's DiLink 4.0 and DiLink 100 infotainment systems — both Android-based platforms with rotating landscape-to-portrait screens — are advanced and feature-rich, but early software versions had known stability issues including random screen freezes, app crashes, slow response times, and Bluetooth connectivity problems. Many of these issues were resolved in subsequent OTA updates. In the UAE, owners of Atto 3 models that did not receive automatic updates due to SIM card or connectivity issues may still be running older software versions. Additionally, the USB-C charging ports in the DiLink ecosystem can develop intermittent connectivity issues when exposed to high humidity and dust — a minor but recurring complaint among Dubai owners. We carry the latest BYD software update files and can perform wired updates for vehicles with OTA reception problems." },
      @{ title = "AC Motor and Power Electronics Heat Soak"; body = "BYD's permanent magnet synchronous motors are highly efficient, but efficiency is not 100% — the lost energy is dissipated as heat in the motor stator, rotor and power electronics. In Dubai, where ambient temperatures are already extreme, the thermal headroom for these components is reduced. Extended high-speed driving on the E11 between Dubai and Abu Dhabi at 120 km/h in 45°C heat can cause some BYD models to reduce peak power output as a protective thermal measure — a behaviour known as thermal derating. This is normal and does not indicate a fault, but if power derating occurs at moderate speeds or in relatively mild conditions, it may indicate that the motor cooling circuit is restricted, the inverter cooling plate has a blockage, or the cooling fan is not functioning correctly. We inspect the complete e-drive thermal circuit at every BYD service." }
    )
    faqs = @(
      @{ q = "How much does BYD servicing cost in Dubai?"; a = "BYD electric vehicles require less routine maintenance than ICE cars — no oil changes, no spark plugs, no timing belts. A standard annual BYD service at FixHive typically costs AED 400–700, covering brake fluid, cabin air filter, wiper blades, tyre rotation, battery health check and a full software and fault code scan. Brake pad replacement is rarely needed due to regenerative braking, and when it is required, it is straightforward and cost-effective." },
      @{ q = "How often should I get my BYD battery health checked in Dubai?"; a = "We recommend an annual battery health check for all BYD EVs driven in Dubai. The check takes approximately 45 minutes and involves logging the battery management system data, checking cell voltage balance, measuring available capacity against original specification, inspecting the thermal management cooling circuit, and verifying that the battery software is on the latest version. Early detection of cell imbalance or cooling inefficiency can prevent accelerated capacity degradation." },
      @{ q = "Does FixHive support BYD OTA updates?"; a = "FixHive stays current with BYD's software release schedule and can perform wired software updates for vehicles that have difficulty receiving OTA updates automatically. We can also advise on which updates are recommended for UAE conditions, check that updates have applied correctly, and restore previous software versions in the rare cases where an update causes a regression." },
      @{ q = "Why is my BYD Atto 3 range lower than the rated figure in Dubai?"; a = "A range reduction of 25–35% versus the WLTP rated figure is entirely normal in Dubai and does not indicate a battery problem. The primary cause is the air conditioning load — running full AC in 45°C heat consumes 2–4 kW continuously. Motorway driving at UAE speed limits (100–130 km/h) also consumes significantly more energy than the mixed-speed test cycle. If your real-world range has declined noticeably compared to your own previous experience — rather than the rated figure — a battery health check is recommended." },
      @{ q = "Can FixHive service my BYD under warranty?"; a = "Yes. UAE consumer protection regulations permit independent garages to perform warranty-compliant scheduled maintenance, provided correct procedures, fluids and OEM-equivalent parts are used. We issue a full service record for every visit. For warranty claims or recall work, the BYD authorised dealer network must be used, but all scheduled servicing can be performed at FixHive without affecting your warranty entitlement." }
    )
    ctaHeading = "Book Your BYD Service in Dubai Today"
    ctaSubtext = "EV-specialist care for BYD Blade Battery vehicles — battery health checks, software updates and complete EV servicing."
